      "text": "To determine the period of the function \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\), we need to analyze the behavior of the individual components \\(\\tan x\\) and \\(\\cot x\\) and then combine their cycles.\n\n1. **Identify the periods of \\(\\tan x\\) and \\(\\cot x\\):**\n   - The function \\(\\tan x\\) has a period of \\(\\pi\\). This means that \\(\\tan(x + \\pi) = \\tan x\\) for all \\(x\\).\n   - The function \\(\\cot x\\) also has a period of \\(\\pi\\). This means that \\(\\cot(x + \\pi) = \\cot x\\) for all \\(x\\).\n\n2. **Determine the period of \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\):**\n   - Since both \\(\\tan x\\) and \\(\\cot x\\) have a period of \\(\\pi\\), the function \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\) will also have a period of \\(\\pi\\). This is because the addition of two functions with the same period will result in a function with the same period.\n\nTherefore, the period of \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\pi}\\).",
