      "text": "Given \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\), we aim to find the period of this function.\n\nFirst, recall the definitions of \\(\\tan x\\) and \\(\\cot x\\):\n\\[\n\\tan x = \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\cot x = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}\n\\]\n\nConsequently,\n\\[\ny = \\tan x + \\cot x = \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} + \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}\n\\]\n\nTo find the period of \\( y \\), we need to determine if there is a positive constant \\( T \\) such that \\( y(x + T) = y(x) \\) for all \\( x \\) in the domain of \\( y \\).\n\nConsider the sum:\n\\[\ny(x) = \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} + \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}\n\\]\n\nWe will test for the period by examining the function in intervals. Let's try \\( T = \\pi \\):\n\\[\ny(x + \\pi) = \\frac{\\sin(x + \\pi)}{\\cos(x + \\pi)} + \\frac{\\cos(x + \\pi)}{\\sin(x + \\pi)}\n\\]\n\nUsing the trigonometric identities:\n\\[\n\\sin(x + \\pi) = -\\sin x \\quad \\text{and} \\quad \\cos(x + \\pi) = -\\cos x\n\\]\n\nSubstitute these into the expression:\n\\[\ny(x + \\pi) = \\frac{-\\sin x}{-\\cos x} + \\frac{-\\cos x}{-\\sin x} = \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} + \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\\[\ny(x + \\pi) = \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} + \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} = y(x)\n\\]\n\nSince \\( y(x + \\pi) = y(x) \\), the function \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\) is periodic with period \\( \\pi \\).\n\nTherefore, the period of \\( y \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\pi}\n\\]",
