      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the period of the function \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\), we need to find the smallest positive value \\( T \\) such that \\( y(x + T) = y(x) \\) for all \\( x \\).\n\nFirst, recall the definitions of the tangent and cotangent functions:\n\\[ \\tan x = \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} \\]\n\\[ \\cot x = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} \\]\n\nThus, the function can be rewritten as:\n\\[ y = \\tan x + \\cot x = \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} + \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} \\]\n\nTo find the period, we need to find the period of \\( \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} + \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} \\). We start by examining the periods of \\( \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} \\) and \\( \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} \\).\n\n1. The function \\( \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\tan x \\) has a period of \\( \\pi \\).\n2. The function \\( \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} = \\cot x \\) also has a period of \\( \\pi \\).\n\nThe sum of two functions with the same period will also have the same period. Therefore, \\( \\tan x + \\cot x \\) has a period of \\( \\pi \\).\n\nTo confirm, we need to show that \\( y(x + \\pi) = y(x) \\):\n\\[ y(x + \\pi) = \\tan(x + \\pi) + \\cot(x + \\pi) = \\tan x + \\cot x = y(x) \\]\n\nThus, the period of \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\pi}\\).",
